    "样本不完整时更适合先补记录，再看趋势" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When samples are incomplete, add records first, then look at trends"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "樣本不完整時更適合先補記錄，再看趨勢"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "样本不足" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Insufficient samples"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "樣本不足"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "样本不足 · 还差 %lld 夜 · Apple Health · SDNN" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Insufficient samples · %lld more nights · Apple Health · SDNN"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "樣本不足 · 還差 %lld 夜 · Apple Health · SDNN"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "样本不足，先继续记录" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Insufficient samples — keep logging first"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "樣本不足，先繼續記錄"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "样本不足时，身体年龄更适合当作一个保守提醒，而不是精确结论。因为它本来就依赖睡眠、活动量、心肺能力和恢复状态等多条线索，如果这些记录缺得比较多，结果就会更容易停留在中性或偏保守的估计。\n\n这时候最重要的不是反复解读数字，而是先补齐记录。比如连续佩戴设备、保证睡眠样本能被记录、补上日常步数和活动数据，再积累几天心肺和静息状态样本。\n\n等样本覆盖更完整后，再去看最近一周的方向，会比现在盯着一个不完整结果更有参考价值。" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When samples are insufficient, body age is better treated as a conservative reminder rather than a precise conclusion. It depends on several clues — sleep, activity level, cardiorespiratory fitness, and recovery — so if many of these records are missing, the result tends to stay at a neutral or conservative estimate.\n\nAt this point the most important thing isn't re-reading the number repeatedly; it's filling in the records first. Wear your device consistently, make sure sleep samples get captured, add daily steps and activity data, and accumulate a few days of cardiorespiratory and resting-state samples.\n\nOnce coverage is more complete, looking at the past week's direction will be far more useful than staring at an incomplete result now."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "樣本不足時，身體年齡更適合當作一個保守提醒，而不是精確結論。因為它本來就依賴睡眠、活動量、心肺能力和恢復狀態等多條線索，如果這些記錄缺得比較多，結果就會更容易停留在中性或偏保守的估計。\n\n這時候最重要的不是反覆解讀數字，而是先補齊記錄。比如連續佩戴裝置、保證睡眠樣本能被記錄、補上日常步數和活動資料，再積累幾天心肺和靜息狀態樣本。\n\n等樣本覆蓋更完整後，再去看最近一週的方向，會比現在盯著一個不完整結果更有參考價值。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "样本不足时，身体年龄更适合当作保守估计；先补齐记录，再看趋势更可靠。" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "With insufficient samples, body age is better treated as a conservative estimate — fill in records first, then trends become more reliable."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "樣本不足時，身體年齡更適合當作保守估計；先補齊記錄，再看趨勢更可靠。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
